#  Configuration file for the Burn unit test
#  Simulation/SimulationMain/unitTest/Burn
#
#  Setup with, for example:
#    ./setup unitTest/Burn -auto -1d +a13 +noio
#
#  The test drives the BurnIntegrate steppers directly and does not evolve the
#  grid, so the mesh exists only to satisfy the framework.  The network is
#  present because the steppers reference Burn_data, whose arrays are sized to
#  NSPECIES; any network will do.

REQUIRES Driver
REQUIRES Grid
REQUIRES physics/sourceTerms/Burn/BurnMain/nuclearBurn
REQUESTS physics/sourceTerms/Burn/unitTest

# The Burn unit references the standard hydrodynamic variable set in its
# initialisation, so declare it even though the test never evolves the mesh.
VARIABLE dens TYPE: PER_VOLUME              # density
VARIABLE temp                               # temperature
VARIABLE pres                               # pressure
VARIABLE eint TYPE: PER_MASS                # specific internal energy
VARIABLE ener TYPE: PER_MASS                # specific total energy
VARIABLE gamc                               # sound-speed gamma
VARIABLE game                               # energy gamma
VARIABLE velx TYPE: PER_MASS                # x-velocity
VARIABLE vely TYPE: PER_MASS                # y-velocity
VARIABLE velz TYPE: PER_MASS                # z-velocity
VARIABLE shok                               # shock detector, read by Burn's shock switch

D sim_initDens   Uniform density used to fill the (unused) mesh
PARAMETER sim_initDens  REAL  1.e7   [ 0.0+ ... ]

D sim_initTemp   Uniform temperature used to fill the (unused) mesh
PARAMETER sim_initTemp  REAL  1.e9   [ 0.0+ ... ]